%I A399986 #12 Oct 26 2026 21:17:20
%S A399986 1,1,1,2,9,52,341,2540,21360,200536,2079837,23618672
%N A399986 The number of distinct 3-inversion sets in the symmetric group on n elements.  A 3-inversion for a permutation w is a set of 3 values appearing in decreasing order in the one-line notation for w.
%C A399986 It appears that this is also the number of size 2 mesh patterns in Table 12 Nr. 59 and 60 of page 25 in “Wilf-Classification of Mesh Patterns of Short Length”. In: The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics 22.4 (Oct. 2015), P4.13. doi: 10.37236/4678 by Hilmarsson, Jónsdóttir, Sigurðardóttir, Lína Viðarsdóttir, Ulfarsson.
%H A399986 Sara Billey, Herman Chau, and Kevin Liu, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.31795">Affine Higher Bruhat Orders</a>, arXiv:2610.31795 [math.CO], oct. 22, 2026.
%H A399986 Ísak Hilmarsson, Ingibjörg Jónsdóttir, Steinunn Sigurðardóttir, Lína Viðarsdóttir, and Henning Ulfarsson, <a href="https://www.combinatorics.org/ojs/index.php/eljc/article/view/v22i4p13">Wilf-classification of mesh patterns of short length</a>, Electron. J. Combin. 22(4) (2015), Art. P4.13.
%e A399986 The 3-inversions of w=[4,3,1,2] are the triples appearing in reverse order, so Inv_3(w)={[1,3,4],[2,3,4]}.  For n=4, the a(4)=9 possible 3-inversion sets among all permutations in S_4 are {}, {[1, 2, 4]}, {[2, 3, 4]}, {[1, 2, 3]}, {[1, 3, 4]}, {[1, 3, 4], [2, 3, 4]}, {[1, 2, 4], [1, 3, 4]}, {[1, 2, 3], [1, 2, 4]}, {[1, 2, 3], [1, 2, 4], [1, 3, 4], [2, 3, 4]}.
%Y A399986 Column k=3 of A399980.
